<title>FINLAND: SKI JUMPING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SKI JUMPING-WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LAHTI, Finland 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results in a</p>
<p>World Cup high hill ski jumping event on Sunday:</p>
<p>Only one round possible because of strong winds:</p>
<p> 1. Andreas Widhoelzl (Austria)	117.9 points (115.5 metres)</p>
<p> 2. Pasi Kytosaho (Finland)	    117.5 (115.0)</p>
<p> 3 equal. Jani Soininen (Finland)    117.0 (115.0)</p>
<p> 3 equal. Kazuyoshi Funaki (Japan)   117.0 (115.0)</p>
<p> 5. Kimmo Savolainen (Finland)	 112.5 (112.5)</p>
<p> 6. Jussi Hautamaki (Finland)	  110.5 (112.5)</p>
<p> 7 equal. Janne Ahonen (Finland)     110.2 (111.5)</p>
<p>7 equal. Kristian Brenden (Norway)  110.2 (111.5)</p>
<p> 9. Roberto Gecon (Italy)		107.4 (110.5)</p>
<p>Leading World Cup standings after 21 events:</p>
<p> 1. Primoz Peterka (Slovenia)	  1,097 points</p>
<p> 2. Dieter Thoma (Germany)		 984</p>
